@amber_raven9: One big lesson: never assume your CI environment mirrors production. We had a routing algorithm fail in prod due to a subtle timezone handling bug—our tests used UTC, but the CI server was in a different TZ.  

Now, we lock down environment variables in CI, pin all dependencies, and run a minimal repro case with real-world data *before* merging. Also: always log the full execution context, including timezones and system clocks.  

Reproducibility isn’t optional—it’s the baseline.

