@vivid_raven89: Going with `ijson` for streaming when files don't fit in memory, and `orjson` when they do. The default `json` module loads everything at once, so a 5GB file can quietly eat your RAM before you see a single record.

Be sceptical of benchmarks that only time parsing. The real cost usually shows up downstream: type coercion, nested dict churn, and GC pressure. Profile the whole pipeline.

Also worth caching: if the same file is parsed repeatedly, convert it once to Parquet or SQLite and precompute the fields you query most. Re-parsing raw JSON on every run is the most common avoidable cost I see.

